()` with timezone-aware `datetime.now(timezone.utc)` across the codebase. Tests must still pass.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-aa28-apikey/omp-928/transcripts/with/trig-omp-fanout/6/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 0, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-aa28-apikey/omp-928/cells/with/trig-omp-fanout/6/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/16.1.5 (/workspace/pi-check/cache2/bin/omp/52843e4fb9bc647bf545b0a658cfab8cc3767330/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "All 5 modules use `from datetime import datetime, timedelta`. Converting every call site at once matters: comparing naive and aware datetimes raises `TypeError` (`cache.Entry.expired`).\nAll 7 `datetime.utcnow()` calls in `app/` now use `datetime.now(timezone.utc)`, and the tests pass (5 of 5). I changed every call at once because comparing a naive datetime with a timezone-aware one raises `TypeError`, and `cache.Entry.expired()` compares two of them.\n\n- **Files:** `audit.py`, `billing.py`, `cache.py`, `reports.py`, `sessions.py`. Each import now reads `from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone`.\n- **Tests:** run with `uv run --no-project --with pytest`, with `DeprecationWarning` turned into an error. A search for `utcnow` finds nothing left.\n\n**One visible output change:** `reports.header()` now ends with a UTC offset, e.g. `T generated 2026-10-13T02:19:02+00:00` instead of `...02:19:02`. The test only checks how the string starts, so it still passes, but anything that parses this exact format would see the difference.\n\n**Also worth knowing:** the values returned by `audit.stamp`, `billing.due_date`, `sessions.new_session` and `reports.generated_at` are now timezone-aware. Any calling code that compares or subtracts them against naive datetimes will raise `TypeError`. Nothing in this repo does that.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 147136, "requests_cache_write": 186967, "requests_cost_usd": 1.0017502, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 22, "requests_output": 1870, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-fanout:claude-opus-5-5:trial6", "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 8, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T02:18:36.270142+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 32.883, "t_checker_s": 0.383, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-fanout", "task_calls": 0, "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1892, "tokens_cache_read": 147136, "tokens_cache_write": 186967, "tokens_fresh": 1892, "tokens_input_uncached": 22, "tokens_main_cache_read": 147136, "tokens_main_cache_write": 186967, "tokens_main_calls": 9, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 22, "tokens_main_output": 1870, "tokens_output": 1870, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 147136, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 186967, "tokens_proxy_calls": 9, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 22, "tokens_proxy_output": 1870, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "trial": 6, "ts_iso": "2026-10-12T19:18:36", "turn_mode": null, "turns": 9, "usage_raw": [{"cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 34967, "cost": {"cache